aom 3.15.3 with Cosmopolitan (scripts/libvips.sh, for the AVIF of vix):

- The headers of Cosmopolitan remove __linux__, so the check of the CPU
  of aarch64 found no method and stopped the build. The method of Linux
  (getauxval) works in Cosmopolitan: it gives 0 on the other systems, and
  then aom uses Neon only.

--- a/aom_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c
+++ b/aom_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c
@@ -127,7 +127,10 @@
   return flags;
 }
 
-#elif defined(__linux__)  // end defined(AOM_USE_ANDROID_CPU_FEATURES)
+// Cosmopolitan removes __linux__ (its programs also run on other
+// systems). Its getauxval() gives the hardware capabilities of Linux, and
+// 0 on the other systems: then only Neon.
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__COSMOPOLITAN__)  // end defined(AOM_USE_ANDROID_CPU_FEATURES)
 
 #include <sys/auxv.h>
 
